# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and fill in the values.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser.

# Google Maps JavaScript API key — the BASEMAP of the Route planner and the
# trip maps, and the PLACE SEARCH in every address field. A browser key by
# design: it is baked into the bundle and read by anyone, so restrict it in the
# Google Cloud console to this app's HTTP referrers (http://localhost:5173/*
# for dev, plus the production origin) and to two APIs: Maps JavaScript API and
# Places API (New). Without the key the maps show a "key not set" notice and
# the search fields fall back to HERE; with the key but without Places enabled,
# only the search fields fall back (one console warning). The HGV overlay
# (HERE's map) works either way.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=

# Routing, truck restrictions, road-snap / reverse geocoding and the HGV
# basemap stay HERE, and the
# HERE API key lives SERVER-SIDE only (server/.env → HERE_API_KEY). The browser
# fetches it at runtime from the auth-gated /api/here/config endpoint, so there
# is intentionally no VITE_HERE_* var here and that key is never baked into
# the frontend bundle.
